[38;5;231m⏺[39m Locked in: FastAPI + SQLite, with ruff, pytest, and mypy set up before feature code. No e2e for now — we can add it
  when there's a UI worth driving.

  Two things left before I can present a design.

  [1mThe fork on auth:[0m this is a team tool, so identity isn't optional, and it's the one decision here with a security
  consequence. Session and token handling is painful to retrofit, so I want your call rather than my default.

  - [1mPassword auth with server sessions[0m — email + password, hashed with Argon2 or bcrypt, opaque session cookie
    (HttpOnly, SameSite). Self-contained, no external dependency, standard and well-understood. Costs: you own password
    reset, lockout, and session expiry.
  - [1mOAuth via a provider[0m (Google/GitHub) — no passwords to store, no reset flow. Costs: an external dependency and app
    registration before anyone can log in locally, which complicates dev and tests.
  - [1mDev-only stub, real auth later[0m — a header or a picker that names the current user, so tasks and notifications can be
    built and tested immediately. Costs: it is genuinely insecure and must never reach a deployment; the real thing is
    a later sub-project.

  I recommend [1mpassword auth with server sessions[0m. It has no external moving parts, keeps tests hermetic, and "team tool"
  means real accounts eventually regardless — the stub just defers the same work while letting an insecure path exist
  in the tree.

  The second question is lighter: how much task there should be in version one.
